    "text": "[2026-09-14T04:13:00Z] Assistant: For a clear and maintainable structure, organize your project as follows:\n\n1. **`src/`**: Place all Rust source files here, with subfolders like `api/` for route handlers and `model/` for data structures.\n2. **`wasm/`**: After running `wasm-pack build`, keep the generated WebAssembly artifacts (`.wasm` and `.js` files) in this folder.\n3. **`frontend/`** (if applicable): Store any client-side code or HTML/CSS that consumes the WebAssembly module.\n4. **`Cargo.toml`** and **`Cargo.lock`** at the root: Manage dependencies with Actix-Web and wasm-bindgen clearly listed.\n5. **`README.md`**: Document setup instructions, key endpoints, and how to run the service locally.\n\nThis layout keeps logic, compilation outputs,",
