    "speaker": "Assistant",
    "text": "[2026-10-26T11:10:00Z] Assistant: Certainly! For testable and maintainable Rust code that integrates seamlessly with WebAssembly, consider adopting a modular architecture where each microservice or component is encapsulated in its own module with well-defined interfaces. Use the `pub` keyword judiciously to expose only necessary functions and types, keeping internal implementations hidden and testable. Additionally, leverage traits to define contracts for reusable functionality across modules, and employ dependency injection where applicable to facilitate unit testing by easily substituting dependencies with mocks or test doubles. This structured approach will enhance both the scalability and testability of your codebase as your project expands.",
