    "speaker": "Elena",
    "text": "[2026-11-16T11:45:00Z] Elena: Hey there! So I've been diving headfirst into building microservices with Rust and WebAssembly, and I'm loving the performance boost—but I'm also feeling a bit overwhelmed. Is it normal to struggle with setting up the right tooling and debugging when you're still getting the hang of it? Any tips from those who've been down this road? And how often do you find yourself balancing work with family time, especially when projects get really intense? Thanks for any advice!",
