    "text": "[2026-11-16T11:55:00Z] Assistant: Sure thing, Elena! A great quick win is to start with a simple \"Hello World\" WebAssembly module that returns a string, then progressively add functionality like basic arithmetic operations or JSON parsing. Completing a small CRUD API for a to-do list using these modules can feel rewarding and provide tangible results without being overwhelming. Plus, you'll get comfortable with the build and deployment pipeline early on. Happy coding!",
