    "question": "What factors did you tell me Marcus should weigh when deciding whether to buy or lease a car for his commute?",
    "ground_truth_answer": "Marcus should consider the following two key factors when deciding between buying and leasing a car for his longer commute:\n\n1. **Total Cost Over Time**:  \n   - **Buying**: Calculate the purchase price, financing costs (interest), insurance premiums, maintenance expenses, and potential resale value. Owning a car outright may lead to higher upfront costs but can be cheaper in the long run if he keeps the vehicle for several years.\n   - **Leasing**: Evaluate the monthly lease payments, any down payment required, insurance costs, and whether the lease includes maintenance (often it does). Leasing typically has lower monthly payments but adds up over time without building equity.\n\n2. **Flexibility and Vehicle Upgrade Cycle**:  \n   - **Buying**: Provides long-term ownership, allowing him to keep the car as long as he wishes or sell it later. However, he’s responsible for all repairs and depreciation.\n   - **Leasing**: Offers the opportunity to drive a newer model every few years with lower upfront costs. This can be advantageous if he prefers having access to the latest technology and doesn’t want to deal with selling or maintaining an older vehicle.\n\nBy weighing these factors—total cost over time and flexibility/upgrade cycle—he can make a decision that aligns best with his financial situation and lifestyle preferences for his longer commute.",
